Partial batch failure needs a decision about failed records and successful siblings. Parking work is a recovery boundary. It does not prove successful processing.

> Do you put the failed event into a DLQ and process it later?

Source: [Q20](/lore/durability-bibliography#q20); [B5](/lore/durability-bibliography#b5-building-event-driven-microservices), [B9](/lore/durability-bibliography#b9-serverless-architectures-on-aws).

## Failure it prevents

A failed item disappears, blocks useful work, or causes successful siblings to run repeatedly.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`PersistedQueue` retains failed records. `DurableQueue` exhaustion can leave its `DurableDeferred` unresolved and the workflow parked. Provide out-of-band repair and requeue.

Source: `packages/effect/src/persistence/PersistedQueue.ts`, `packages/effect/src/workflow/DurableQueue.ts`.

## How to check

Exhaust an item, find its failure record, repair it, and prove redrive resumes the intended waiter without repeating successful siblings. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Retry needs idempotent effects](/lore/retry-needs-idempotency), [Golden signals expose overload](/lore/golden-signals-expose-overload).

